    {
      "id": "fb-002",
      "question": "How are SIM bundles managed?",
      "shape": "document",
      "guard": "fix",
      "blocked_on": null,
      "asked_as": "1a1db65e-52d5-493b-a1a9-7e495005530a",
      "http_status": 200,
      "seconds": 38.06,
      "answer": "SIM bundles are managed through the SIM Cards module, which handles several key aspects:\n\n1. **SIM Inventory Management**: It maintains a complete inventory of SIM cards, including details like ICCID, MSISDN, IMEI pairing, telco, tariff plan, current asset, status, and country. This helps in controlling costs and reducing orphaned subscriptions.\n\n2. **Telco and APN Management**: It manages telco relationships and APN profiles, ensuring seamless connectivity.\n\n3. **Data Bundles and Roaming**: The module tracks data bundles and roaming, preventing surprise bills and maintaining communication continuity.\n\n4. **Signal Quality and Cost Visibility**: It provides visibility into signal quality and costs, helping to prevent silent outages.\n\n5. **Suspend and Reactivate Actions**: The module allows for the suspension and reactivation of SIM cards as needed.\n\n6. **Evidence-Grade Mapping**: It maps SIMs to devices, assets, and countries, ensuring accurate connectivity management.\n\nThis management approach helps both service providers and end-user enterprises maintain communication continuity for vehicles, people, cargo, generators, and remote equipment.\n\nSource: OLIWA User Stories — this is the documented design; I can't confirm from here which parts are live.",
