    {
      "id": "fb-004",
      "question": "What is IVMS?",
      "shape": "document",
      "guard": "fix",
      "blocked_on": null,
      "asked_as": "1a1db65e-52d5-493b-a1a9-7e495005530a",
      "http_status": 200,
      "seconds": 36.51,
      "answer": "IVMS, or In-Vehicle Monitoring System, is a vehicle telematics solution that provides a minimum telemetry set including GPS data (latitude/longitude, speed, heading, timestamp), connectivity information (GSM, satellites, HDOP/PDOP), and power status (external voltage, internal battery if supported). It also includes ignition/ACC status. The system is designed to track vehicles with recommended policies for normal tracking intervals and offline thresholds to catch faults early. Preventative maintenance is advised, such as weekly checks on the most offline units and monthly audits for ignition wiring issues.\n\nSource: NAVAS CMS User Manual — this is the documented design.",
